Old Irish Accountant, and also got from him one of my very best stories,

430
00:57:53,330 --> 00:57:56,730
which is not something to take lightly.

431
00:57:56,730 --> 00:58:05,400
As sat in, Marvin Coyle was a great preacher on the beatitudes of decentralization,

432
00:58:05,400 --> 00:58:07,400
not virtues, beatitudes.

433
00:58:07,400 --> 00:58:11,960
So I sat in his office there on the beatitudes,

434
00:58:11,960 --> 00:58:15,960
And suddenly there was a telex which was next to the spittoon.

435
00:58:15,960 --> 00:58:19,780
It began to yammer and that turned around and it said,

436
00:58:19,780 --> 00:58:22,240
Pete, don't pay any attention to it.

437
00:58:22,240 --> 00:58:27,240
That's only the Kansas City plant manager telexing in that he's going out to lunch

438
00:58:27,240 --> 00:58:31,240
and kept on telling me about the total autonomy of local management.

439
00:58:35,890 --> 00:58:38,890
Very few people to whom I owe that good a story.

440
00:58:38,890 --> 00:59:08,530
But also, I thought I knew things, you know, he was an old, nasty, tough, but he had a

441
00:59:08,530 --> 00:59:09,530
better brain.

442
00:59:09,530 --> 00:59:19,270
He had done a great deal of things, and he had realized that this decentralization approach

443
00:59:19,270 --> 00:59:26,270
of him worked only where you could really set up a genuine business with its own P&L

444
00:59:26,270 --> 00:59:28,270
and its own model.

445
00:59:28,270 --> 00:59:41,630
and that therefore Chevrolet could not be decentralized, but also that that big a unit

446
00:59:41,630 --> 00:59:47,550
but commercially fully competitive could not and did not develop that.
